.TH SDL_GetCurrentThreadID 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetCurrentThreadID \- Get the thread identifier for the current thread.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_thread.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_ThreadID SDL_GetCurrentThreadID(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This thread identifier is as reported by the underlying operating system\[char46] If SDL is running on a platform that does not support threads the return value will always be zero\[char46]
.PP
This function also returns a valid thread ID when called from the main thread\[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the ID of the current thread\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetThreadID (3)
